# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# audio-lab .gitignore
# Root is the source of truth; pipeline/ and spotify/ keep their own too
# (git applies all of them cumulatively).
# Intent: track source, lockfiles, transcripts, notes, and cover/chapter
# art; NEVER track secrets, personal data, virtualenvs, or heavy media.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets, tokens & credentials — never ────────────────────
.env
.env.*
.envrc                       # direnv (often holds exported keys)
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
token.json
*token*.json
*secret*
*credential*
# Spotify / spotipy OAuth caches — plain AND username-suffixed (.cache-jared)
.cache
.cache-*
.spotify_cache
# Google / GCP service-account keys (common Google-TTS / STT leak vector)
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
application_default_credentials.json
gcloud-*.json
# Cloud / TTS provider creds you may add later
.aws/
azure.json
elevenlabs.json

# ── Personal data exports (PII) ──────────────────────────────
data/
MyData/
# Spotify "download your data" dumps (classic + extended formats)
StreamingHistory*.json
Streaming_History*.json
endsong*.json
Payments.json
Identifiers.json
Userdata.json
Inferences.json

# ── Generated audio, video & data ────────────────────────────
#
# WHAT THESE RULES ARE FOR: keeping WORKING media out — voice auditions, test
# renders, stems, tempo experiments. There are 141 such files under output/ and
# that is the volume this block exists to hold back.
#
# WHAT THEY ARE NOT FOR: the finished episode. A published episode master is
# distributed to the whole world on a podcast feed and on YouTube; treating it
# as something that must not enter a repository was never a decision anyone
# made, it was a side effect of a pattern written for scratch files.
#
# That side effect cost real work. `*.mp4` silently swallowed BOTH YouTube
# masters (told-straight-ep01.mp4, told-straight-ep02.mp4) for ten days --
# `git add` skips an ignored path without a word, so nobody saw it fail. They
# survived only because they happened to still be sitting in a home folder.
# Maintainer decision 2026-08-02: finished masters are tracked. See the
# carve-outs at the bottom of this block.
output/
# Audio
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.wav
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.aac
*.aiff
*.aif
*.wma
# Video
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv
# Archives (data dumps, model bundles)
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
# Design source files (Adobe Illustrator etc.) — heavy binary, never tracked;
# the exported *.png deliverables are tracked, the editable source is not.
*.ai

# ── Finished episode deliverables are TRACKED ────────────────
# Cover and chapter art (*.png), transcripts (*.md/*.txt/*.vtt/*.html),
# captions and show notes were always tracked. As of 2026-08-02 the finished
# audio and video masters are too -- these are the published artifacts, not
# working files. Anything still being iterated on stays in output/, which is
# ignored wholesale above and is unaffected by these carve-outs.
!episodes/**/*.mp3
!episodes/**/*.mp4

# Guardrail, not a limit: nothing here approaches GitHub's 100 MB ceiling
# (largest master today is 15.7 MB). If a finished master ever exceeds 75 MB,
# raise it with the maintainer before committing rather than inventing a
# storage scheme for a problem that has not happened.

# ── ML / transcription model blobs (e.g. local Whisper) ──────
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.gguf
models/

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
# ...but episode build-provenance SCRIPTS under episodes/*/build/ ARE tracked.
# The slashless `build/` above (Python packaging) would otherwise swallow them.
# Same convention holds for the upcoming E1/E2 rebuilds. Only .py/.md are
# re-included — NOT .ai (Illustrator source saved here stays ignored via *.ai).
!episodes/*/build/
!episodes/*/build/*.py
!episodes/*/build/*.md
dist/
wheels/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Working artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────
# Most of artifacts/ is session scratch (handoffs, walkthroughs, research notes)
# and stays untracked. But PM-authored executor specs and issue drafts are TRACKED
# on purpose: a spec written to a gitignored path never reaches a cold-start, cloud,
# or fresh-clone session — the exact failure AGENTS.md is itself tracked to avoid.
# macos-system-health tracks artifacts/specs/ for the same reason.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/specs/
!artifacts/issues/
# Session scratch stays ignored by contract:
artifacts/walkthroughs/
artifacts/session-handoffs/

# ── Logs & temp ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
tmp/
*.tmp

# ── Editors / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*                          # macOS resource forks
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/

# ── Claude Code ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore machine-local settings, but allow the shared, committed
# settings.json (your cross-repo permission-continuity practice).
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/*
